  // vehicle-wheel-info) was exactly this class. (method 220 wvehicle)
  // un-held, falcon-wheels rung (wheel-
  // constants leg): its own s2+192 wall was a handle-verified process
  // typed only to the base "process" class rather than process-drawable;
  // type_casts.jsonc casts it, stack_structures.jsonc covers its own two
  // local scratches, and it decodes clean with no warnings. Removed from
  // this list.
  // (method 217 wvehicle) and (method 218 wvehicle) UN-HELD, wheelreal
  // rung: both were held on an unresolved local stack struct (each its
  // own "Failed to guess stack use for 16"); a fresh scoped decode of
  // wvehicle alone (allowed_objects wvehicle, no pre-existing casts)
  // walked every op touching the sp+16 region in both raw disassemblies
