  // is jak3's wvehicle-method-164 shape field-for-field (a rigid-body
  // matrix at 0, five composed quaternions at 64/80/96/112/128, two
  // constant vectors (1 0 0 1)/(0 1 0 1) at 144/160, a probe vector at 176
  // and a transform-target vector at 192), landed as
  // wvehicle-method-217-work; 208-239 (32 bytes) is read and written by
  // nothing in the function's own body and is declared padding. This also
  // resolves the prior note's "264-byte arg2 struct with fields at
  // 16/32/36/40/44/48/52/56/80" claim: those offsets are vehicle-wheel-
  // info's own already-typed fields (arg1), not the local struct, and the
  // local struct itself measures 244 bytes (0xf4), not 264. (method 218
  // wvehicle)'s own local struct shares (method 217 wvehicle)'s matrix/
  // quaternion core at the same offsets but carries a wider vector bank
  // (nine vectors total against 217's four) plus a five-float tail at
  // 320-336, one of which (an asin-based arc term over arg1's own travel
  // and susp-arm-length fields) has no jak3 twin at all; landed as
  // wvehicle-method-218-work, size 340 bytes (0x154). The prior note's
  // "field read at offset 144... attributed to nothing" does not hold
  // against this rung's own trace: gp+144 is written by a local-pos copy
  // at op 66-69 and read back both as a full quad (op 111-114, op
  // 246-249) and as a lone scalar at its own +4 byte (op 180, the y
  // component, feeding the arc-term formula); the prior rung's read must
