    "end-end-credits",
    // title-control-init/title-control-spawn: UNPARKED (titleobs lane). The
    // original raw-label-leak (L215 in title-control-init's
    // external-art-buffer callback) is gone now that dma-get-named-buffer
    // has a real defun (goal_src/jakx/engine/dma/lobby-dma.gc, landed since
    // this park was written) and anonymous_function_types.jsonc's title-obs
    // index 30 is retyped from the placeholder (function object object) to
    // (function external-art-buffer object), matching the field type
    // external-art-buffer's own init-heap slot already declares. The
    // remaining "Bad register dependency on a0" on both functions was not a
    // second raw-label defect: the register trace shows title-control-spawn
    // reading a genuine caller-supplied a0 at function entry and forwarding
    // it into title-control-init via run-function-in-process, so both
    // externs gained a real (symbol) arg0 instead of the zero-arg
    // placeholder. Both now decode with zero warnings (title-control-spawn
    // keeps one pre-existing, harmless "Return type mismatch int vs
    // object", the same class already accepted elsewhere in this file, e.g.
    // relocate's "process vs title-control").
    // draw-language-select: decodes to seemingly complete GOAL text ("may
    // read a0" was the only decode-time flag) but fails real compilation
    // with a raw label leak (an unresolved anon-function) or return-type
    // mismatches that trace back to the same unresolved inner lambda;
    // parked as asm. Out of this lane's scope (title-control-spawn's own
    // band does not call it).
    "draw-language-select",
    // desarena-obs: desarena-activate/deactivate never decoded at all
    // ("no type analysis"), no in-band call-site evidence (nothing in
    // this object calls them; they are level-hook functions referenced
    // from elsewhere, out of this band's scope).
    "desarena-activate",
    "desarena-deactivate",
    // palm-tree's own methods 11/52/54/55: all raw, unconverted register
    // dumps reading a1/uninitialized locals with no traceable source
    // (method 55: "add failed uninitialized integer 16" plus a stack-use
    // guess failure; method 54: raw l.q load; method 11 and 52: fully
    // unconverted). method 52 is called from (post idle palm-tree), which
    // still resolves fine against a parked method's decoder-generated
    // stub body.
    "(method 11 palm-tree)",
    "(method 52 palm-tree)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree)",
    "(method 55 palm-tree)",
    // palm-tree-a/b/c's own method 35 and 54 overrides (six total): the
    // same "may read a1 not set" pattern as the base type's method 54
    // (a1 is very likely a vector impact-velocity/direction argument, but
    // no in-band evidence pins the exact signature since every one of
    // these bodies reads it uninitialized rather than receiving it as a
    // declared param).
    "(method 35 palm-tree-a)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-a)",
    "(method 35 palm-tree-b)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-b)",
    "(method 35 palm-tree-c)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-c)",
    // (enter explode-into-nothing wvehicle) and (enter explode wvehicle),
    // internal names (anon-function 16 wvehicle-states) and (anon-function
    // 18 wvehicle-states): asm_functions_by_name is consulted before
    // state-handler recognition renames the function, so the internal name
    // is the key that matches here (same shape as (anon-function 6
    // credits-obs) above). Both bodies build an explosion-init-params
    // struct and fully resolve (stack struct, both handle fields, the
    // ppointer-chase type prop) except for the low-level "sllv reg, reg,
    // r0" step that folds the resolved ppointer into the handle's low
    // 32 bits: the decompiler's handle idiom matcher only recognizes that
    // shift when its source is already handle-typed (the direct
    // field-load case, e.g. (post sink wvehicle)'s wheel-handle loop in
    // this same file), not when the source is a (pointer process) freshly
    // produced by a ppointer chase, which is what process->handle's own
    // inline expansion produces here. Same failure class as (method 10
    // rigid-body-queue) below (raw "sllv reg, reg, r0" triple the macro
    // matcher does not recognize); parked as asm rather than hand-folded
    // since both bodies are large (128+ and 352+ stack bytes) and the only
    // unresolved piece is this one bit-twiddle, not the surrounding logic.
    "(anon-function 16 wvehicle-states)",
    "(anon-function 18 wvehicle-states)",
    // (anon-function 44 script), the 'send-event script-form command's own
    // lambda: builds a stack event-message-block (stack_structures.jsonc
    // entry above) then relays it through an actor-group's raw entry array
    // (gp-0 + s3-1*8 + 12, the same computed-pointer idiom jak3's own
    // identically-purposed function uses to reach a raw process pointer).
    // jak3's version reads that pointer's "child" field once and indexes it
    // (3) to reach the process it wants; jakx's compiled body instead does
    // two further loads off it (offset 20, then offset 12 of that result),
    // and connection's own field layout only explains the first one
    // (param1, basic-typed, offset-assert 20): the second load (offset 12
    // of a generically basic-typed value) has no declared field this rung's
    // evidence can point to, and no call site in this function's own body
    // pins the runtime type. types2's "Could not figure out load" throws
    // before type_casts.jsonc is ever consulted for that op (same
    // ForwardProp.cpp mechanism cited for plow's launch-nearby-players
    // above), so no cast resolves it. Every other part of this function
    // (the event-message-block construction, the eval! dispatch loop, the
    // actor-group-vs-single-process cond) is fully clean, config-fixed
    // evidence and stays in place.
    "(anon-function 44 script)",
    // (anon-function 33 script): calls local-human-player-above-height?, a
    // symbol with no defun or extern anywhere in goal_src (jak1/2/3/jakx)
    // and no jak3 twin to transplant from (script.gc's own decode-error
    // history, commit 9c2db1970, already identified this as an unresolved
    // net-player-family Unknown symbol, held for that family's own pilot
    // rather than guessed here). type_casts.jsonc cannot invent a binding
    // for an undeclared symbol.
    "(anon-function 33 script)",
    // (anon-function 39/40 script): "Stack slot load mismatch" is raised by
    // decompiler/analysis/stack_spill.cpp's StackSpillMap, a fully
    // automatic scan with no config hook (confirmed by reading the source,
    // same finding as commit 9c2db1970): once a 4-byte access claims a
    // stack offset, a later 16-byte access at the same offset is rejected
    // outright, and stack_structures.jsonc governs a different mechanism
    // (unknown_stack_structure_tag) that does not reach this check.
    "(anon-function 39 script)",
    "(anon-function 40 script)"
  ],
